From: Shirogane Tsumugi <artoriapendragon123@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/sysfb: simpledrm: free the firmware framebuffer on
 takeover

U-Boot leaves the boot logo in a /reserved-memory carveout that simpledrm
scans out until the real sun4i-drm stack loads.  Without help that carveout
stays reserved for the life of the system -- ~1.8M gone on a 64M board.

Let the firmware opt in to getting it back: if the simple-framebuffer node
carries srgn,free-on-takeover, hand the pages to the page allocator when
simpledrm is removed (which is exactly the aperture eviction the real DRM
driver performs while taking over).  Requires the carveout to not be
no-map, so the pages still have their struct page and linear mapping;
free_reserved_area() is the same mechanism that frees initrd memory.

The PageReserved check keeps a mis-described carveout (no-map after all,
or no reserved-memory node) from corrupting the buddy lists -- U-Boot and
the kernel are separate projects, so treat the FDT as a system boundary.

Signed-off-by: Shirogane Tsumugi <artoriapendragon123@gmail.com>

---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/sysfb/simpledrm.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/sysfb/simpledrm.c
index 7a95d2dac..a56dba54b 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/sysfb/simpledrm.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/sysfb/simpledrm.c
@@ -3,6 +3,7 @@
 #include <linux/aperture.h>
 #include <linux/clk.h>
 #include <linux/minmax.h>
+#include <linux/mm.h>
 #include <linux/of_address.h>
 #include <linux/of_clk.h>
 #include <linux/of_reserved_mem.h>
@@ -856,12 +857,51 @@ static int simpledrm_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	return 0;
 }
 
+/*
+ * The firmware can mark its framebuffer carveout as disposable: once the
+ * real DRM driver kicks simpledrm out (this remove path), the pages go
+ * back to the page allocator instead of staying reserved forever. Only
+ * works when the /reserved-memory node has no "no-map" -- the pages must
+ * still have their struct page and linear mapping. On a 64M board the
+ * ~1.8M framebuffer is worth the trouble.
+ */
+static void simpledrm_free_fb_on_takeover(struct platform_device *pdev)
+{
+	struct device_node *np = pdev->dev.of_node;
+	struct resource *res;
+	phys_addr_t start, end;
+
+	if (!np || !of_property_read_bool(np, "srgn,free-on-takeover"))
+		return;
+
+	res = platform_get_resource(pdev, IORESOURCE_MEM, 0);
+	if (!res)
+		return;
+
+	/* only whole pages the carveout fully owns */
+	start = PAGE_ALIGN(res->start);
+	end = (res->end + 1) & PAGE_MASK;
+	if (start >= end || !pfn_valid(PHYS_PFN(start)))
+		return;
+
+	/*
+	 * Not a memblock carveout after all (no reserved-memory node, or
+	 * no-map, or already freed): freeing would corrupt the buddy lists.
+	 */
+	if (!PageReserved(pfn_to_page(PHYS_PFN(start))))
+		return;
+
+	free_reserved_area(phys_to_virt(start), phys_to_virt(end), -1,
+			   "simpledrm framebuffer");
+}
+
 static void simpledrm_remove(struct platform_device *pdev)
 {
 	struct simpledrm_device *sdev = platform_get_drvdata(pdev);
 	struct drm_device *dev = &sdev->sysfb.dev;
 
 	drm_dev_unplug(dev);
+	simpledrm_free_fb_on_takeover(pdev);
 }
 
 static const struct of_device_id simpledrm_of_match_table[] = {
